    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Property Shop are delighted to present 32 Ard Righ Road, a charming red-brick period home ideally positioned on one of Stoneybatter`s most sought-after streets.This handsome property enjoys an abundance of character, generous living accommodation and excellent curb appeal. Lovingly maintained by the current owners, and benefits from new windows and doors, while retaining the warmth and charm synonymous with period properties.\r\nThe accommodation extends to a welcoming entrance hallway, lounge, living room, kitchen/dining room and full bathroom at ground floor level. Upstairs are two generously proportioned double bedrooms, providing excellent bedroom accommodation.To the rear, the property boasts a generous east-facing yard, while on-street parking is available to the front. The home is further complemented by gas-fired central heating and generous overall floor space.\r\nThe location is exceptional, with all that Stoneybatter has to offer right on the doorstep. A vibrant and increasingly popular neighbourhood, Stoneybatter is renowned for its excellent selection of independent cafés, restaurants, bars and local shops, along with a choice of supermarkets and a range of primary and secondary schools.Smithfield, Phibsborough, TU Dublin`s Grangegorman campus and Dublin city centre are all within easy walking distance. The area is also exceptionally well served by public transport, with numerous Dublin Bus routes nearby and convenient access to the Luas at Grangegorman, Smithfield and Museum.\r\nA wonderful opportunity to acquire a characterful period home in one of Dublin`s most desirable and well-connected neighbourhoods. Early viewing is highly recommended to appreciate all that this fine home has to offer. Viewing are by appointment only through our Manor Street office.\r\n\r\nHallway 2.96m (9'9\") x 1.13m (3'8\")\r\nWelcoming hallway with wood flooring & dado rail.\r\n\r\nLounge 3.4m (11'2\") x 3.08m (10'1\")\r\nThe original parlour room located to the front of the property, open fire.\r\n\r\nLiving Room 3.28m (10'9\") x 4.68m (15'4\")\r\nTo the rear of the property with laminate wood flooring.\r\n\r\nKitchen 4.78m (15'8\") x 2.7m (8'10\")\r\nExtended kitchen with room to dine, fitted eye & floor level units, access to the rear patio yard.\r\n\r\nBathroom 1.37m (4'6\") x 2.63m (8'8\")\r\nFull bathroom located to the rear of the property.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 2.91m (9'7\") x 4.67m (15'4\")\r\nLarge double bedroom located to the front of the property with vaulted ceilings, original polished wood flooring and built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 3.5m (11'6\") x 3.61m (11'10\")\r\nA second double bedroom to the rear with original polished wood flooring.\r\n\r\nExterior 2.91m (9'7\") x 1.77m (5'10\")\r\nAn East facing patio garden to the rear, on street resident`s disc parking to the front.\r\n\r\nArea \r\nApprox 77 Sq Mts / 829 Sq Ft"
      },
